{
  "title": "Brachial Plexus",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/anatomy/10052/brachial-plexus",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jan 3 2022",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Standard: C5, C6, C7, C8, T1 – 77% of patients",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Prefixed: Prefixed (contributions from C3, C4) – 22%",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Postfixed (roots caudal to T1) – 1%",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Remember: Robert Turner Drinks Cold Beer",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Roots (5)**: ventral rami of C5-T1, superior and posterior to subclavian",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "dorsal scapular nerve (C5): through levator scapula to supply levator scapula, rhomboid major & minor",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "long thoracic nerve (C5, 6, 7): posterior to plexus onto thoracic wall to supply serratus anterior",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Trunks (3):** emerge from triangle formed by anterior scalene, middle scalene, first rib",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "superior (C5,6 roots)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "suprascapular nerve (C5, 6): through suprascapular notch to supraspinatus, infraspinatus, AC and glenohumeral joints",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "nerve to subclavius (C5, 6)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "middle (C7)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "inferior (C8, T1)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Divisions (6):** 3 anterior, 3 posterior (each trunk gives 1 anterior and 1 posterior division)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Cords (3):**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Posterior Cord: formed from 3 posterior division",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "upper subscapular nerve (C5, 6): subscapularis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lower subscapular nerve (C5,6): subscapularis, teres major",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "thoracodorsal nerve (C6, 7, 8): latissmus dorsi",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Lateral Cord: ant divisions of superior & middle trunks (C5, 6, 7)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lateral pectoral nerve (C5, 6, 7): pectoralis major, communication with medial pectoral nerve",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Medial Cord: anterior division of inferior trunk (C8, T1) Branches (6) – 2 terminal branches from each cord",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "medial pectoral nerve (C8, T1): pierces pec minor; supplies pec minor and major",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial brachial cutaneous nerve (T1)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial antebrachial cutaneous nerve (C8, T1)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Posterior cord:",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "axillary nerve (C5, 6): through quadrilateral space to teres minor, deltoid, major nerve supply to glenohumeral joint, superior lateral brachial cutaneous nerve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "radial nerve (C5 – T1): runs with long head of triceps (triangular interval) into radial groove on posterior humerus; supplies elbow & forearm extensors, supinator; posterior brachial cutaneous, inferior lateral brachial cutaneous, posterior antebrachial cutaneous, superficial radial (post. radial hand)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Lateral cord:",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "lateral cord of median nerve (C5 – C7): joins medial cord anterior to axillary artery then travels with artery: wrist flexors (except FCU, ulnar ½ FDP), pronators, radial two lumbricals, OP, APB, superficial head FPB); sensory distribution in hand",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "musculocutaneous (C5, 6, 7): most superficial branch, pierces coracobrachialis (1.5-9 cm from origin) to supply biceps, coracobrachialis, brachialis, ends as lateral antebrachial cutaneous nerve",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "Medial cord:",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "medial cord of median nerve (C8, T1): see above",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ulnar nerve (C8, T1): FCU, ½ FDP, adductor pollicus, deep head FPB, hypothenar, intrinics (except radial 2 lumbricals), sensory to hand",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
